1
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:15,829
JE GEUN-U
HAN YEONG-HUI

2
00:00:16,996 --> 00:00:19,165
When I was in high school,

3
00:00:19,249 --> 00:00:22,585
my mother drove into the ocean
with my father in the car.

4
00:00:25,296 --> 00:00:27,215
My mom made it out of the water,

5
00:00:28,007 --> 00:00:29,134
but my poor father

6
00:00:29,759 --> 00:00:33,596
is probably still wandering alone
somewhere in the deep ocean.

7
00:00:35,765 --> 00:00:38,726
The fingernails my crazy mom left me.

8
00:00:39,227 --> 00:00:43,439
That's when I knew it wasn't an accident.

9
00:00:43,523 --> 00:00:46,484
-Don't you think it was insurance fraud?
-That's what I'm saying.

10
00:00:47,152 --> 00:00:50,029
It was both suicide and murder,

11
00:00:50,113 --> 00:00:52,031
but I said nothing.

12
00:00:52,866 --> 00:00:54,701
I was still too young

13
00:00:55,368 --> 00:00:56,828
to bear all of it.

14
00:00:57,745 --> 00:01:00,707
How could I have ever lived a normal life?

15
00:01:03,251 --> 00:01:04,711
A severe panic disorder.

16
00:01:05,211 --> 00:01:08,840
From that day on, I couldn't go outside
without my medication.

17
00:01:08,923 --> 00:01:11,926
But even with it,
I still wouldn't go outside.

18
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:15,013
A happy and peaceful confinement.

19
00:01:16,389 --> 00:01:19,517
Maybe that's when people started

20
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:24,147
to see me as a rat hiding in a hole.

21
00:01:31,112 --> 00:01:33,031
This is the Hangang River area

22
00:01:33,114 --> 00:01:35,700
where a woman in her early thirties
was found dead.

23
00:01:35,783 --> 00:01:37,535
Authorities are identifying the woman,

24
00:01:37,619 --> 00:01:41,915
but they were unable to find any leads,
including family or acquaintances.

25
00:01:41,998 --> 00:01:44,918
The entire area
was temporarily closed off…

26
00:01:45,001 --> 00:01:46,377
I

27
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:49,297
still can't go outside.

28
00:01:52,675 --> 00:01:55,553
The world goes on just fine without me.

29
00:01:57,305 --> 00:01:58,556
For the past three years,

30
00:01:59,057 --> 00:02:01,601
while I've been trapped in this house,

31
00:02:01,684 --> 00:02:05,438
the world has been just as lively as ever,

32
00:02:06,272 --> 00:02:07,857
every single day.

33
00:02:11,527 --> 00:02:12,862
Damn it.

34
00:02:13,738 --> 00:02:16,032
It just won't fall apart.

35
00:02:19,118 --> 00:02:22,497
While I'm stuck here,
popping pills for my panic disorder.

36
00:02:32,507 --> 00:02:35,218
YOUR ORDER IS PLACED!
ARRIVING TOMORROW MORNING (SAT)

37
00:04:10,772 --> 00:04:14,734
People go around
calling me a genius writer.

38
00:04:15,234 --> 00:04:19,781
A reclusive writer shrouded in mystery,
known only by a pen name,

39
00:04:19,864 --> 00:04:22,533
with neither a face nor a real name.

40
00:04:28,831 --> 00:04:33,211
A mysterious new writer
who burst onto the scene like a comet,

41
00:04:33,294 --> 00:04:35,421
releasing one hit novel after another.

42
00:04:43,304 --> 00:04:44,389
A comet?

43
00:04:46,391 --> 00:04:49,644
At least comets
can roam through space freely.

44
00:05:03,699 --> 00:05:05,159
Fuck.

45
00:05:06,953 --> 00:05:08,579
They know nothing.

46
00:05:33,729 --> 00:05:35,481
Moon-jae!

47
00:05:39,026 --> 00:05:41,320
Moon-jae!

48
00:05:44,323 --> 00:05:46,492
Moon-jae!

49
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:52,790
Moon-jae!

50
00:06:05,428 --> 00:06:07,472
Moon-jae!

51
00:06:10,266 --> 00:06:11,601
Moon-jae!

52
00:06:16,439 --> 00:06:18,566
The same nightmare every night.

53
00:06:19,859 --> 00:06:21,986
The same panic attack every day.

54
00:06:23,029 --> 00:06:26,157
Nothing ever changes.

55
00:07:10,159 --> 00:07:11,786
Let's see

56
00:07:12,495 --> 00:07:15,373
if anything has changed since yesterday.

57
00:07:16,666 --> 00:07:18,209
Yakult.

58
00:07:20,294 --> 00:07:22,255
The mailman. Saying hello.

59
00:07:24,173 --> 00:07:25,341
I'm here at the scene in…

60
00:07:25,424 --> 00:07:27,093
The same news.

61
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:30,137
Maybe the outside world

62
00:07:30,888 --> 00:07:32,890
really is a simulation.

63
00:07:33,391 --> 00:07:35,893
…where a woman was found dead yesterday.

64
00:07:35,977 --> 00:07:39,605
This is usually a quiet neighborhood, but…

65
00:07:39,689 --> 00:07:41,148
I'm so sick of it all.

66
00:07:41,232 --> 00:07:43,901
…and investigators flooded the area,

67
00:07:43,985 --> 00:07:47,154
tensions remained high for some time.

68
00:07:48,281 --> 00:07:51,284
The victim was found
with severe external injuries.

69
00:07:51,367 --> 00:07:55,663
Police have secured CCTV footage
of a suspect leaving the scene

70
00:07:55,746 --> 00:07:58,791
and are working
to identify and track the individual.

71
00:08:08,843 --> 00:08:10,303
BARO BANK

72
00:08:13,973 --> 00:08:15,349
BARO BANK CERTIFICATE

73
00:08:16,142 --> 00:08:16,976
Huh?

74
00:08:21,188 --> 00:08:22,857
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

75
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:25,818
What the hell?

76
00:08:31,365 --> 00:08:32,533
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

77
00:08:32,617 --> 00:08:34,702
TOO MANY FAILED ATTEMPTS
ENTER YOUR PIN

78
00:08:49,425 --> 00:08:50,509
What was that?

79
00:08:58,976 --> 00:09:00,227
Is this a bug?

80
00:09:10,571 --> 00:09:13,616
DONGBU POLICE STATION

81
00:09:17,119 --> 00:09:18,037
You're here.

82
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,246
Where have you been?

83
00:09:19,955 --> 00:09:21,082
The courthouse?

84
00:09:22,291 --> 00:09:23,751
Is that still going on?

85
00:09:25,878 --> 00:09:28,172
Hey. Get to work.

86
00:09:28,255 --> 00:09:30,216
I'm working. Covering your part too.

87
00:09:30,299 --> 00:09:32,468
Fuck, we're already short-handed as hell.

88
00:09:37,848 --> 00:09:39,600
-Morning, sir.
-Hey.

89
00:09:39,684 --> 00:09:40,685
Sir.

90
00:09:40,768 --> 00:09:42,269
You little punk.

91
00:09:42,812 --> 00:09:45,022
Where have you been? The courthouse?

92
00:09:45,898 --> 00:09:49,151
At least tell me where you're going
before you disappear, punk!

93
00:09:49,235 --> 00:09:52,113
A freaking cop, going in and out
of domestic violence court?

94
00:09:53,322 --> 00:09:55,074
It wasn't violence.

95
00:09:55,157 --> 00:09:58,494
All I did was punch the wall once.

96
00:09:58,577 --> 00:10:01,247
That's violence, punk. Against the wall.

97
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:02,957
Yeah, nice going.

98
00:10:03,958 --> 00:10:04,792
Hey.

99
00:10:06,961 --> 00:10:09,004
Just get to work.

100
00:10:09,088 --> 00:10:10,256
You get to work.

101
00:10:10,339 --> 00:10:11,757
Gonna work or what, punks?

102
00:10:20,391 --> 00:10:21,434
Hey, you.

103
00:10:22,601 --> 00:10:24,145
Looks like you got a tip.

104
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:26,981
A tip?

105
00:10:27,064 --> 00:10:29,817
Yeah. Might be about the body found
in the Hangang River.

106
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:30,735
But why you?

107
00:10:31,318 --> 00:10:32,611
Is it someone you know?

108
00:10:33,988 --> 00:10:34,989
Who sent it?

109
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:36,365
It's anonymous.

110
00:10:36,949 --> 00:10:38,367
Then why ask if I knew them?

111
00:10:38,451 --> 00:10:40,411
I was talking about the bastard in there.

112
00:10:40,494 --> 00:10:42,371
Oh, someone's in here?

113
00:10:42,455 --> 00:10:44,373
Huh? Jesus.

114
00:10:49,128 --> 00:10:51,505
THE BODY FOUND IN THE HANGANG RIVER
WAS NOT A SUICIDE

115
00:10:56,135 --> 00:10:58,220
KIM YEONG-GEUN
APT 704, BLDG 104, CENTUM HEIGHTS FORE

116
00:11:02,516 --> 00:11:03,559
You know that guy?

117
00:11:03,642 --> 00:11:05,102
No. Never seen him before.

118
00:11:06,145 --> 00:11:08,105
There must be a reason this came to you.

119
00:11:08,189 --> 00:11:12,526
Who mails stuff like this these days?
They'd just post it online.

120
00:11:13,652 --> 00:11:15,863
So who killed themselves
in the Hangang River?

121
00:11:16,363 --> 00:11:17,948
How would I know, punk?

122
00:11:18,616 --> 00:11:20,785
Yeah, you find out. It was sent to you.

123
00:11:20,868 --> 00:11:22,578
-Take care, sir.
-Where are you going?

124
00:11:22,661 --> 00:11:24,288
-Who is this?
-Seriously!

125
00:11:24,789 --> 00:11:26,999
How the hell would I find out? Seriously…

126
00:11:27,082 --> 00:11:28,667
-Hey, kid.
-Sir?

127
00:11:29,335 --> 00:11:30,878
Run a background check.

128
00:11:31,378 --> 00:11:33,756
Name, Kim Yeong-geun. ID number…

129
00:11:36,258 --> 00:11:37,134
Find out.

130
00:11:39,428 --> 00:11:40,471
Yes, sir.

131
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,281
TO SON SOO-HYUN

132
00:12:01,367 --> 00:12:02,868
APT 704, BLDG 104
CENTUM HEIGHTS FORE

133
00:12:18,759 --> 00:12:22,429
You call me over way too often
just because I'm nearby.

134
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:25,307
You know, you sure use a lot of gas.

135
00:12:26,016 --> 00:12:27,434
You got a cold or something?

136
00:12:27,935 --> 00:12:30,229
How would I catch a cold?

137
00:12:30,312 --> 00:12:32,439
I never go outside.

138
00:12:32,523 --> 00:12:34,483
Unless you give it to me.

139
00:12:38,654 --> 00:12:39,488
Hey.

140
00:12:40,739 --> 00:12:41,824
What's that?

141
00:12:43,993 --> 00:12:44,952
It's a bug.

142
00:12:45,035 --> 00:12:46,412
A bug.

143
00:12:57,172 --> 00:12:58,591
I saved my number in there.

144
00:12:58,674 --> 00:13:00,759
You don't have anyone else to call anyway.

145
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:04,513
But this thing was working perfectly fine,
wasn't it?

146
00:13:05,848 --> 00:13:07,182
You watched porn?

147
00:13:07,766 --> 00:13:08,976
Shut up.

148
00:13:10,895 --> 00:13:13,022
Then why is it acting up all of a sudden?

149
00:13:13,105 --> 00:13:15,524
I know. The fingerprint isn't working,

150
00:13:15,608 --> 00:13:17,610
so I can't make payments or anything.

151
00:13:17,693 --> 00:13:20,529
You got it for me a few months ago.
Why does it keep acting up?

152
00:13:21,363 --> 00:13:22,865
Hey, show me your fingers.

153
00:13:24,325 --> 00:13:26,827
Maybe you wrote so much,
your fingerprints wore off.

154
00:13:27,786 --> 00:13:29,705
Having fun? Huh?

155
00:13:32,207 --> 00:13:33,042
Hey.

156
00:13:33,542 --> 00:13:35,961
If it's urgent,
I can pay for it for you now.

157
00:13:36,045 --> 00:13:37,671
Everything in the cart, right?

158
00:13:37,755 --> 00:13:38,589
Yeah.

159
00:13:39,089 --> 00:13:40,966
Oh, and the OTP is in there,

160
00:13:41,050 --> 00:13:43,469
so just set up your fingerprint
in the banking app.

161
00:13:43,552 --> 00:13:45,804
Man, you really are a handful.

162
00:13:45,888 --> 00:13:47,014
You got a better idea?

163
00:13:47,097 --> 00:13:50,059
The accounts are all in your name,
and all the money's with you.

164
00:13:50,142 --> 00:13:53,103
Your money's safe, so don't worry.

165
00:13:53,187 --> 00:13:54,396
Anything else?

166
00:13:54,939 --> 00:13:56,023
That.

167
00:13:56,649 --> 00:13:58,651
I'll call someone to take care of it.

168
00:14:01,987 --> 00:14:04,823
Every day's been the same for me.

169
00:14:04,907 --> 00:14:06,909
Why's all this happening today?

170
00:14:06,992 --> 00:14:07,910
Oh man.

171
00:14:07,993 --> 00:14:08,827
Who knows?

172
00:14:08,911 --> 00:14:11,830
Maybe the phone and the glass
were all part of the plan.

173
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:17,419
Isn't that the simulation theory?
The story you wrote.

174
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:22,800
Hey, the protagonist
was manipulated into believing that.

175
00:14:22,883 --> 00:14:24,051
Did you actually read it?

176
00:14:24,134 --> 00:14:25,928
I bought it, punk. Isn't that enough?

177
00:14:26,011 --> 00:14:29,056
You expect me to actually read
the whole thing too?

178
00:14:29,765 --> 00:14:30,724
What about your meds?

179
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:32,935
-Do you have enough?
-Yeah, I've still got some.

180
00:14:33,602 --> 00:14:35,396
All right, then.

181
00:14:36,063 --> 00:14:39,900
Thanks to you,
I've gotta play a panic disorder patient.

182
00:14:39,984 --> 00:14:41,360
I'm getting good at acting.

183
00:14:41,443 --> 00:14:42,820
Was that all?

184
00:14:44,071 --> 00:14:45,781
Yeah. You're leaving already?

185
00:14:45,864 --> 00:14:47,950
Accountants don't just sit around all day.

186
00:14:48,450 --> 00:14:50,327
There's our school reunion today too.

187
00:14:50,411 --> 00:14:51,620
I'm busy as hell.

188
00:14:51,704 --> 00:14:53,163
You guys still get together?

189
00:14:53,247 --> 00:14:54,748
You're the only one not coming.

190
00:14:54,832 --> 00:14:56,917
All the guys who made a bit of money
show up.

191
00:14:57,001 --> 00:14:59,712
Man, that shitty high school.

192
00:14:59,795 --> 00:15:02,381
Reunion, my ass.
Aren't you sick of it already?

193
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:06,510
And you aren't sick of being stuck here?
It's been three years already.

194
00:15:06,593 --> 00:15:07,803
I mean, besides me,

195
00:15:08,303 --> 00:15:09,680
nobody else comes to see you.

196
00:15:10,723 --> 00:15:12,224
Of course I'm sick of it.

197
00:15:14,184 --> 00:15:16,437
You said you'd get me out of here. When?

198
00:15:17,271 --> 00:15:18,564
Yeah, you will.

199
00:15:19,523 --> 00:15:23,527
You'll feel better once you're somewhere
with beaches, palm trees, and all that.

200
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:29,491
Just wait. I'll get you out of here soon.

201
00:15:32,244 --> 00:15:33,078
Bye now.

202
00:15:34,830 --> 00:15:37,541
-When are you coming back?
-Call me if anything happens.

203
00:15:38,042 --> 00:15:39,460
I'll come right away.

204
00:15:40,878 --> 00:15:41,879
Hey.

205
00:16:20,209 --> 00:16:23,921
BARO BANK CERTIFICATE
FINGERPRINT NOT MATCHED

206
00:16:32,304 --> 00:16:34,098
What the hell is wrong with this again?

207
00:17:36,034 --> 00:17:36,869
Who is it?

208
00:17:36,952 --> 00:17:39,037
Oh, yes. I'm with the police.

209
00:17:47,004 --> 00:17:48,338
What brings you here?

210
00:17:48,422 --> 00:17:51,341
Well, we've got a report.
Mr. Kim Yeong-geun?

211
00:17:52,801 --> 00:17:54,094
No.

212
00:17:54,178 --> 00:17:55,762
-You're not?
-No, I'm not.

213
00:17:57,139 --> 00:17:58,265
Doesn't he live here?

214
00:17:59,099 --> 00:18:01,727
No. No one by that name does.

215
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:03,562
Damn.

216
00:18:04,354 --> 00:18:06,064
We've got a report, and…

217
00:18:06,857 --> 00:18:08,609
Can I take a quick look around?

218
00:18:11,778 --> 00:18:13,405
-Sure. Go ahead.
-All right.

219
00:18:13,488 --> 00:18:15,240
This won't take long.

220
00:18:18,368 --> 00:18:19,745
Oh wow.

221
00:18:19,828 --> 00:18:21,830
This place is huge.

222
00:18:24,208 --> 00:18:26,043
Oh, a bird flew into it.

223
00:18:27,961 --> 00:18:29,087
A bird?

224
00:18:29,588 --> 00:18:32,132
There are still birds
flying into these things, huh?

225
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,176
Strange.

226
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,053
That must've hurt.

227
00:18:38,639 --> 00:18:39,806
Do you live alone?

228
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:40,724
Yes.

229
00:18:46,855 --> 00:18:49,900
Wow, this is a really nice place.

230
00:18:54,112 --> 00:18:56,615
If you've confirmed they're not here,

231
00:18:56,698 --> 00:18:58,408
please leave now.

232
00:18:58,909 --> 00:19:01,912
Sure, I was gonna leave anyway.

233
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:15,592
It said Kim Yeong-geun lives here.

234
00:19:15,676 --> 00:19:17,344
Who's that person anyway?

235
00:19:17,427 --> 00:19:18,637
No idea.

236
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:21,181
Who knows? He might be hiding here.

237
00:19:36,989 --> 00:19:38,073
Fine, then. Look.

238
00:19:39,741 --> 00:19:41,827
Thank you for your cooperation.

239
00:19:52,296 --> 00:19:53,130
Are you done?

240
00:19:54,256 --> 00:19:55,382
Please leave now.

241
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:08,353
Sure, sorry to bother you.

242
00:20:14,443 --> 00:20:15,277
By the way,

243
00:20:16,737 --> 00:20:18,405
what do you do?

244
00:20:23,368 --> 00:20:25,495
Yeah, the tip was just a prank.

245
00:20:25,579 --> 00:20:27,581
Kim Yeong-geun doesn't even live there.

246
00:20:27,664 --> 00:20:30,375
What did he say again?
Just some writer lives there.

247
00:20:30,459 --> 00:20:32,294
Did you identify the deceased?

248
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:34,713
How am I supposed to?
They're unidentified.

249
00:20:34,796 --> 00:20:35,672
Who's that thug?

250
00:20:35,756 --> 00:20:37,424
How the fuck should I know?

251
00:20:37,507 --> 00:20:39,217
We don't even know where he lives.

252
00:20:39,301 --> 00:20:40,135
Just with a photo?

253
00:20:40,218 --> 00:20:41,928
-This punk.
-Am I a fucking FBI agent?

254
00:20:42,012 --> 00:20:43,847
I don't know, punk. Figure it out!

255
00:20:43,930 --> 00:20:46,850
-Hang up. I'm going to the chief's office.
-Hello? Damn it.

256
00:20:47,351 --> 00:20:49,686
For fuck's sake. Seriously.

257
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:57,194
PARK SUN-YONG

258
00:20:57,277 --> 00:20:58,820
But why me?

259
00:20:59,654 --> 00:21:01,656
Who the hell sent it?

260
00:21:08,455 --> 00:21:11,166
IS THIS THE RIGHT OTP?

261
00:21:11,249 --> 00:21:12,542
SON SOO-HYUN

262
00:21:33,105 --> 00:21:36,233
RISING STAR, FACELESS GENIUS WRITER
KNOWN ONLY BY HIS PEN NAME

263
00:21:36,316 --> 00:21:39,528
"INTERVIEW" AUTHOR SUSPENDS SERIALIZATION
DUE TO PANIC DISORDER

264
00:21:39,611 --> 00:21:41,780
2 YEARS AFTER VANISHING
WITHOUT EXPLANATION

265
00:21:41,863 --> 00:21:43,115
AN IRRESPONSIBLE ESCAPE?

266
00:21:43,198 --> 00:21:46,326
NEW NOVEL "EVIL ALWAYS PREVAILS"
SET FOR HOLLYWOOD ADAPTATION

