Don't you have a credit card? Or cash?

357
00:30:01,487 --> 00:30:03,031
Hold on. Just a moment.

358
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:06,492
Come on. Take a better look.

359
00:30:11,372 --> 00:30:12,832
Hey! Wait!

360
00:30:14,876 --> 00:30:17,629
Hey, you! Stop right there!

361
00:30:17,712 --> 00:30:18,630
Hey!

362
00:30:41,194 --> 00:30:42,779
-Have you been well?
-Yes, sir.

363
00:30:43,571 --> 00:30:45,323
-Please take a seat.
-Sure.

364
00:30:57,961 --> 00:31:02,799
2025 SOONGAM HIGH SCHOOL
13TH ALUMNI REUNION

365
00:31:02,882 --> 00:31:04,092
You need to keep it up.

366
00:31:04,175 --> 00:31:05,301
That's dedication.

367
00:31:08,012 --> 00:31:09,931
You need to take care of yourself now.

368
00:31:10,014 --> 00:31:11,099
Huh?

369
00:31:14,811 --> 00:31:16,729
Who are you? Sir?

370
00:31:19,899 --> 00:31:21,776
Where's Soo-hyun? Son Soo-hyun?

371
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:23,236
Son Soo-hyun?

372
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,863
He's on a business trip abroad.

373
00:31:25,947 --> 00:31:28,324
Cut the crap. He said he'd be here today.

374
00:31:30,118 --> 00:31:31,494
Anyway, who…

375
00:31:34,038 --> 00:31:35,039
You don't know me?

376
00:31:35,581 --> 00:31:37,458
I'm Moon-jae. Je Moon-jae.

377
00:31:38,167 --> 00:31:39,252
Don't you remember me?

378
00:31:39,794 --> 00:31:41,879
-Is that really Je Moon-jae?
-I don't think so.

379
00:31:44,132 --> 00:31:45,091
You.

380
00:31:46,467 --> 00:31:49,262
Aren't you Min-seok?
The class president in our second year?

381
00:31:49,345 --> 00:31:50,179
Right? It's you.

382
00:31:50,263 --> 00:31:52,432
You always prayed before exams.

383
00:31:52,932 --> 00:31:53,766
Where's Soo-hyun?

384
00:31:54,851 --> 00:31:56,811
I mean, yeah, he's Min-seok, but…

385
00:32:01,983 --> 00:32:03,526
I don't think you're Moon-jae.

386
00:32:03,609 --> 00:32:06,112
Because I had a drink with Moon-jae
last week.

387
00:32:06,195 --> 00:32:08,281
He came to the last reunion too.

388
00:32:08,990 --> 00:32:09,824
Didn't he?

389
00:32:09,907 --> 00:32:11,284
What are you talking about?

390
00:32:11,367 --> 00:32:13,244
I haven't left the house in three years.

391
00:32:13,327 --> 00:32:15,079
What are you doing? Who are you?

392
00:32:16,497 --> 00:32:17,582
I'm Moon-jae.

393
00:32:17,665 --> 00:32:20,960
-No, you're not Moon-jae.
-I'm Moon-jae. Je Moon-jae!

394
00:32:27,341 --> 00:32:30,470
Something only a classmate would know…
He's Kyeong-tae.

395
00:32:31,054 --> 00:32:32,972
Forgot his last name. Top of the class.

396
00:32:33,056 --> 00:32:35,516
That's Kwon Yong-hyeon.
We used to play basketball.

397
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:37,351
Beside him, our math teacher. Gestapo!

398
00:32:37,435 --> 00:32:39,479
All right. Calm down.

399
00:32:39,562 --> 00:32:41,189
Is he really Mr. Je Moon-jae?

400
00:32:41,272 --> 00:32:42,148
No.

401
00:32:42,231 --> 00:32:45,151
I see Moon-jae all the time.
He's not Moon-jae.

402
00:32:46,027 --> 00:32:49,947
I was Moon-jae's homeroom teacher
in his second year.

403
00:32:50,031 --> 00:32:52,492
We even met at the last reunion.

404
00:32:52,575 --> 00:32:54,660
Hey, who are you?

405
00:32:54,744 --> 00:32:56,204
Why pretend to be Moon-jae?

406
00:32:56,954 --> 00:32:58,081
Let's calm down.

407
00:32:58,956 --> 00:33:00,917
Any proof of identity? Maybe an ID card?

408
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,127
I came out like this.
I didn't bring anything.

409
00:33:03,211 --> 00:33:05,296
-I was in a rush.
-You've got your phone.

410
00:33:05,379 --> 00:33:08,674
Everyone keeps their ID
on their phone these days.

411
00:33:10,885 --> 00:33:14,430
This phone is not under my name. I…

412
00:33:15,890 --> 00:33:18,893
I'm not really in a position
to have things in my name right now.

413
00:33:18,976 --> 00:33:21,062
Like a house or a bank account…

414
00:33:21,145 --> 00:33:22,563
Then who are you?

415
00:33:29,779 --> 00:33:31,197
Goddamn it.

416
00:33:32,073 --> 00:33:34,575
I came to meet my friend.
Why are you taking me?

417
00:33:34,659 --> 00:33:37,328
I said we'll talk at the station.
Watch your foot.

418
00:33:54,387 --> 00:33:55,221
That…

419
00:34:04,397 --> 00:34:05,523
That's…

420
00:34:09,110 --> 00:34:10,111
Wait a second.

421
00:34:10,194 --> 00:34:11,320
Sit properly.

422
00:34:11,404 --> 00:34:12,280
We'll talk there.

423
00:34:20,371 --> 00:34:25,376
Last night, a man believed to be homeless
was found dead in a vacant lot in Seoul…

424
00:34:25,459 --> 00:34:28,171
Once we confirm your identity,
you can go. Just wait.

425
00:34:28,254 --> 00:34:31,716
The man had no identification on him,
so his identity has not…

426
00:34:31,799 --> 00:34:33,467
People are so out of it these days.

427
00:34:34,051 --> 00:34:35,469
Shouldn't he be drug tested?

428
00:34:35,553 --> 00:34:37,471
…and living conditions worsen,

429
00:34:37,555 --> 00:34:41,726
safety concerns are growing
for vulnerable people on the streets.

430
00:34:41,809 --> 00:34:44,729
Nothing comes up.
The ID number doesn't exist either.

431
00:34:44,812 --> 00:34:45,771
What?

432
00:34:45,855 --> 00:34:48,065
A man was found lying motionless…

433
00:34:48,149 --> 00:34:50,193
There's no match for his fingerprints.

434
00:34:50,276 --> 00:34:52,486
He must be an illegal immigrant
or a ghost.

435
00:34:52,570 --> 00:34:54,363
Come on. That can't be.

436
00:34:55,072 --> 00:34:56,824
His fingerprints aren't in the system?

437
00:34:58,701 --> 00:35:00,203
-Nothing comes up.
-Huh?

438
00:35:00,286 --> 00:35:01,913
…believed to be in his fifties.

439
00:35:01,996 --> 00:35:03,915
When he was discovered,

440
00:35:03,998 --> 00:35:06,667
he was lightly dressed
and had no identification on him.

441
00:35:07,418 --> 00:35:08,878
-What the hell?
-Where did he go?

442
00:35:08,961 --> 00:35:10,338
-Oh man.
-Damn it.

443
00:35:51,879 --> 00:35:54,465
Come on, why are you asking me that?

444
00:35:54,548 --> 00:35:58,010
I mean, I didn't do that.
So why is it like that, then?

445
00:35:58,094 --> 00:36:01,347
Like I said, it says
it was re-registered two months ago.

446
00:36:01,430 --> 00:36:03,140
The ID number and the fingerprints.

447
00:36:03,224 --> 00:36:06,477
Who changed it without my permission?

448
00:36:07,520 --> 00:36:10,189
-Mr. Je Moon-jae did!
-I'm Je Moon-jae. Seriously!

449
00:36:11,607 --> 00:36:12,650
What's going on?

450
00:36:14,986 --> 00:36:16,821
We've got a difficult one here.

451
00:36:16,904 --> 00:36:20,616
How can I just take your word for it?
You have nothing to prove it.

452
00:36:20,700 --> 00:36:24,245
You can't re-register
unless you're the person yourself.

453
00:36:24,328 --> 00:36:25,204
I told you already.

454
00:36:27,123 --> 00:36:28,708
I'm Je Moon-jae.

455
00:36:28,791 --> 00:36:31,711
And I never re-registered.

456
00:36:31,794 --> 00:36:33,671
I don't know about that.

457
00:36:33,754 --> 00:36:36,966
It only says
it was re-registered two months ago

458
00:36:37,049 --> 00:36:39,510
due to a personal data breach

459
00:36:39,593 --> 00:36:41,762
by Mr. Je Moon-jae himself.

460
00:36:46,058 --> 00:36:48,102
In that case,

461
00:36:48,728 --> 00:36:50,688
could my friend have changed it?

462
00:36:50,771 --> 00:36:54,358
I already told you.
Only the person themselves can do it.

463
00:36:55,318 --> 00:36:57,653
I never did that.

464
00:37:03,159 --> 00:37:05,369
Isn't there a photo there or something?

465
00:37:05,453 --> 00:37:06,787
It should be… Let me see.

466
00:37:06,871 --> 00:37:07,872
What are you doing?

467
00:37:07,955 --> 00:37:09,498
Sir!

468
00:37:09,582 --> 00:37:10,750
-Sir, calm down.
-Hold on.

469
00:37:10,833 --> 00:37:13,085
-Calm down, sir!
-I'm Je Moon-jae!

470
00:37:14,337 --> 00:37:15,379
I'm Je Moon-jae!

471
00:37:23,304 --> 00:37:24,722
Shouldn't we catch him?

472
00:37:31,854 --> 00:37:35,608
How can I just take your word for it?
You have nothing to prove it.

473
00:38:43,217 --> 00:38:44,051
What the…

474
00:39:12,872 --> 00:39:14,123
I'm sorry.

475
00:39:30,431 --> 00:39:31,432
I left

476
00:39:32,057 --> 00:39:33,309
my meds at home.

477
00:39:46,780 --> 00:39:47,907
What are you doing here?

478
00:39:49,492 --> 00:39:50,326
Huh?

479
00:39:53,078 --> 00:39:54,663
Why are you back?

480
00:39:54,747 --> 00:39:56,540
Did you leave something behind?

481
00:39:57,166 --> 00:39:58,334
What do you mean?

482
00:39:58,918 --> 00:40:01,170
You took your stuff
and said goodbye earlier.

483
00:40:01,670 --> 00:40:03,923
You also replaced that window in a flash.

484
00:40:05,549 --> 00:40:10,179
It's a floor-to-ceiling window.
Replacing it takes days.

485
00:40:12,932 --> 00:40:15,684
I did this?

486
00:40:15,768 --> 00:40:16,810
Yes.

487
00:40:24,360 --> 00:40:28,197
Did you happen to see anything
on the ground down there?

488
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:30,032
Like a dead bird or something.

489
00:40:32,117 --> 00:40:33,244
A bird?

490
00:40:33,869 --> 00:40:34,828
I don't think so.

491
00:40:35,454 --> 00:40:38,958
The security office is right below,
so I would've seen it.

492
00:41:06,026 --> 00:41:08,487
Other unclaimed remains
don't get any attention.

493
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:11,031
The police, the media…
She's one famous lady.

494
00:41:11,115 --> 00:41:12,741
She was on the news too.

495
00:41:12,825 --> 00:41:15,035
An unidentified body found
in the Hangang River.

496
00:41:15,119 --> 00:41:17,496
Autopsy's done. No signs of foul play.

497
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:20,457
-So why are the cops involved again?
-We received a tip.

498
00:41:21,041 --> 00:41:22,668
Better not look. She drowned.

499
00:41:31,051 --> 00:41:35,389
She was perfectly fine,
and suddenly she's unidentified?

500
00:41:35,889 --> 00:41:37,308
Is that even possible?

501
00:41:37,391 --> 00:41:39,184
Three bodies like that in here alone.

502
00:41:39,268 --> 00:41:40,603
Unclaimed or unidentified.

503
00:41:40,686 --> 00:41:42,354
There are a lot more nationwide.

504
00:41:42,438 --> 00:41:45,065
No fingerprint match.
She could be a foreigner.

505
00:42:03,876 --> 00:42:05,878
AUTOPSY ROOM
RESTRICTED AREA

506
00:42:14,511 --> 00:42:15,554
Hello?

507
00:42:17,264 --> 00:42:18,182
Where?

508
00:42:20,809 --> 00:42:22,144
Who from Violent Crimes?

509
00:42:26,398 --> 00:42:29,526
Han-su from Criminal Investigations
said you're after Kim Yeong-geun.

510
00:42:29,610 --> 00:42:31,403
I'm busting my ass looking for him.

511
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:34,865
But there's nothing.

512
00:42:34,948 --> 00:42:36,784
No fucking criminal record or anything.

513
00:42:37,368 --> 00:42:39,453
That's right.
Because he's never been caught.

514
00:42:40,579 --> 00:42:42,122
He was known for being ruthless,

515
00:42:42,206 --> 00:42:45,501
mixed up in illegal gambling,
loan sharking, and all that.

516
00:42:45,584 --> 00:42:48,379
He made bank off illegal gambling sites
a few years back.

517
00:42:48,879 --> 00:42:50,798
Thugs know how to sniff out money.

518
00:42:50,881 --> 00:42:53,759
But they call him Noja. You know, Laozi.

519
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:56,845
Like Confucius and Mencius.

520
00:42:57,429 --> 00:42:59,139
-Noja?
-He hasn't been around lately.

521
00:42:59,223 --> 00:43:00,432
We're after him too.

522
00:43:01,225 --> 00:43:02,309
What did the tip say?

523
00:43:02,893 --> 00:43:07,564
Something about him and the woman
found dead in the Hangang River.

524
00:43:07,648 --> 00:43:10,984
But I can't investigate without a lead.

525
00:43:11,068 --> 00:43:12,194
A woman?

526
00:43:12,945 --> 00:43:15,531
As far as I know,
he only dealt with gang stuff.

527
00:43:21,412 --> 00:43:26,375
They said he's basically
their version of Internal Affairs.

528
00:43:30,087 --> 00:43:31,255
Yeong-geun.

529
00:43:31,964 --> 00:43:32,965
Yeong-geun!

530
00:43:33,048 --> 00:43:35,259
How could you do this to me?

531
00:43:48,689 --> 00:43:52,901
He tosses money into the grave
when he buries troublemakers in the gang.

532
00:43:52,985 --> 00:43:55,404
That's another reason
they call him "Noja."

533
00:43:56,238 --> 00:43:58,866
You know, as in the money
they send the dead off with.

534
00:43:59,867 --> 00:44:03,162
Everyone scattered
after the gang fell apart,

535
00:44:03,704 --> 00:44:05,205
but he's still scary.

536
00:44:05,706 --> 00:44:07,499
Be careful when you go after him.

537
00:44:10,711 --> 00:44:13,338
What a load of shit. He's just a thug.

538
00:44:38,238 --> 00:44:39,364
ACCOUNTANT SON SOO-HYUN

539
00:44:49,041 --> 00:44:51,668
Sir! You can't park here!

540
00:44:52,544 --> 00:44:53,504
You need to move…

541
00:44:58,425 --> 00:45:00,135
Isn't that a baseball bat?

542
00:45:27,830 --> 00:45:28,664
Noja?

543
00:45:28,747 --> 00:45:30,624
You fucking bastard.

544
00:46:50,871 --> 00:46:52,164
Damn it.

545
00:48:13,870 --> 00:48:16,081
You probably need some time to settle in.

546
00:48:16,999 --> 00:48:19,960
The doctor said take one
if you feel suffocated or anxious.

547
00:48:22,462 --> 00:48:24,798
You've gotta toughen up mentally.

548
00:48:25,382 --> 00:48:27,467
You'll have to hide here for a while.

549
00:48:27,551 --> 00:48:28,760
Will we…

550
00:48:31,138 --> 00:48:31,972
be okay?

551
00:48:33,557 --> 00:48:35,600
We'll be fine. Just trust me.

552
00:49:47,214 --> 00:49:48,673
Who am I?

553
00:49:52,594 --> 00:49:53,428
You wanna know?

554
00:54:30,497 --> 00:54:33,416
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang

